th Trump's backing behind her.\n\nMoney tells a similar story: McKinney has raised roughly $1 million and benefits from more than $2 million in outside support, while Duresky has raised under $200,000 with no outside help. The only available poll, conducted in February by a Republican-sponsored firm, showed the Republican ahead by thirteen points. Prediction markets give Duresky roughly a seven percent chance. A Republican hold is the clear expectation, with the main uncertainty stemming from the open seat and Democratic hopes tied to a favorable national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.71}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0347, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0403, "margin": -13.5}]}